module Darklang.Cli.Docs.Live

let content () : String =
  """# Live: running things follow your edits

Save an edit and the things running it change, the moment the save passes
the checker. A broken save never blanks anything: the last good version keeps
running with the error beside it.

## A live view

Any module with these three is a view:

  module My.Counter
  type Model = { count: Int }
  type Msg = | Inc
  let init () : Model = Model { count = 0 }
  let update (m: Model) (e: Darklang.Cli.Apps.Host.Event<Msg>) : Model = ...
  let render (m: Model) : Stdlib.Cli.UI.Node.Node<Msg> =
    Stdlib.Cli.UI.Node.column [ Stdlib.Cli.UI.Node.bold "counter"; ... ]

  apps view My.Counter --live   open it, following your edits to `render` or anything it calls
                                from another terminal and it repaints

The tree `render` returns paints to the terminal, to a page, or to text, so
the same view is a pane and a web page. Ctrl-S saves the model as a `val`;
`apps view My.Counter --resume <val>` starts from it.

## A live server

  serve My.router               every request runs the newest router that
                                passes its checks; a broken save keeps the
                                previous one serving and logs why
  serve My.router --live        follow edits; the open page reloads when its code changes
  serve My.router               pin the version resolved at start

Each request is a process: a slow handler holds up nobody, one past
`http.requestTimeoutMs` is cancelled with a 504, one that raises answers 500
with its error, one stopped from `ps` answers 503.

## A live host on another machine

  # there
  dark --branch feature apps enable sync    pull the branch on an interval
  dark --branch feature serve My.router
  # here
  config set live.autopush on               every save commits and pushes
  # ... edit, save; the page there changes a few seconds later

## Live values in the editor

The workbench and the LSP show `// = value` beside the calls in a function:
its last recorded trace, replayed through the code as it is now. Edit a callee,
the values follow, no new call needed. Any recorded trace will do: the default
recording keeps every impure call, and the pure ones are recomputed.

## What a save prints

  dark val My.Counter.title '"v2"'
  ✓ Updated value My.Counter.title
    My.Counter.render follows
  dark val My.Counter.title 3
  ! Updated value My.Counter.title
    My.Counter.render no longer type-checks: expected String, got Int (argument 2)

A view on the broken version shows a band under its last good frame:
`My.Counter.render: still on the last good version; the newest has a type
error: ...`. Fix it and the band goes.

The rule underneath: reload is name resolution. A save binds a name to a new
hash, the old hash stays, a host resolves its entries again on the next
change. `docs processes` is the other half; the design is `docs/live.md` in
the repository.
"""
